12> While vs. Do-While: Provide a code example where a do...while loop would behave differently than a standard while loop with the same condition.

The key difference is:
A while loop checks the condition before executing, while a do...while loop executes once before checking the condition.

For example, suppose the condition is already false:
Using while
let number = 10;

while (number < 5) {
    console.log("Number:", number);
    number++;
}

There is no output because JavaScript checks:
number < 5

which means:
10 < 5 → false

Therefore, the loop body never executes.
Using do...while
Now use the same condition:
let number = 10;

do {
    console.log("Number:", number);
    number++;
} while (number < 5);

Output:
Number: 10

Even though 10 < 5 is false, the code executes once because the condition isn't checked until after the loop body runs.
So the execution order is:
while:

Check condition
      ↓
If true
      ↓
Run code

Compared with:
do...while:

Run code
     ↓
Check condition
     ↓
If true → run code again

Therefore, do...while guarantees at least one execution, whereas a regular while loop can execute zero times if its condition is false from the beginning.

